## Rules Hardening & Closed-Loop Directives (Locked)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The following 4 rules in `@[.agents/rules/01-python-backend.md]` have been physically updated to permanently close all AI bypass loopholes:

1. **`idiomatic_pattern_matching`**: Explicitly bans `case dict()` and `case {"key": ...}` patterns on raw untyped dictionaries; mandates that `match/case` is used exclusively on strictly typed Pydantic models, Enums, and Discriminated Unions.
2. **`duck_typing_token_shield_ban`**: Banning `extra="ignore"` and `extra="allow"` unconditionally on ALL Pydantic models across the codebase; bans the creation or classification of "Token Shields".
3. **`pydantic_configuration_enforcement`**: Enforces `model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid", strict=True)` on ALL Domain Models, DTOs, and schemas without exception.
4. **`strict_attribute_integrity`**: Banned `if "key" in raw_dict:` or `if key in dict:` checks for duck-typing. The `in` operator is restricted exclusively to typed collection membership testing.

